- Always keep your file searches focused exclusively on the source code and active asset directories. Ignore any build folders, compiled outputs, or temporary files.
- Version milestones (v4.x.*.*): sync package.json (build filename source of truth), js/core/config.js, js/core/main.js, js/core/Game.js (game orchestrator), js/ui/HUD.js (in-game #version-label) and index.html (tab title) to the same version, and keep the check.mjs [6aa] version-sync gate green before committing.
- Runtime Verification (v3.85.0): The authoritative gates are `node tools/check.mjs` (ALL GREEN) and `node tools/verify-bundle.mjs` (Bundle OK) — always run these. To additionally live-verify a built bundle WITHOUT violating the No-Screenshots rule, serve `Builds/Kitty Vs Everything <ver>.html` over a local HTTP server (the Playwright browser blocks `file://`) and inspect it **text-only**: console errors + accessibility DOM snapshot + `browser_evaluate` for DOM state (e.g. nameplate text, active dot index). NEVER capture or view screenshots/images. Kill the server (by port) and delete any temp `serve.mjs` afterward so the working tree stays clean.
- Hazards module (v3.97.0, `js/hazards/`): the hazard field is INDEPENDENT — `HazardManager` owns its own spawner/list/FX state (ticked by Game.js as `game.hazards.update(this, dt)` + `game.hazards.draw(this, ctx)`), separate from WaveManager, DropManager, enemies and easter eggs. Hazards are non-lootable: `js/hazards/` modules must NEVER import the DropManager or drop power-ups. All tunable stats (speed/hp/radius/score/proximityFuse/explosion + spawner cadence/weights) live ONLY in `HAZARD_TYPES`/`HAZARD` in `js/core/config/hazards.js` (re-exported by `config.js`) — hazard modules must not hardcode them. Hazards only take damage on-screen (v3.83.0 off-screen kill gate parity); destruction routes through `HazardManager.explode(game, hz, { byPlayer })` (player kills score, self-detonations don't; both drop nothing). Hazard sprites: 256×256 PNGs in `C:\AI-GAMES\.assets\Hazards\`, manifest keys `hazard_<type>` with `Hazards/` subfolder values in `tools/asset-manifest.json` (importer supports subfolder prefixes since v3.97.0).
- Hangar exact-scale preview (v3.98.0): `HANGAR_ZOOM` in `js/core/main.js` is **1.0** — the hangar hero renders the catship at its EXACT in-game scale (70px frame × `MAIN_SHIP_SCALE`, same `drawSpriteShip` pipeline as `PlayerRenderer`). Never re-introduce a showcase zoom multiplier; `tools/check/sections/06ag-crisp-rendering.mjs` pins the `const HANGAR_ZOOM = 1.0;` literal.
- Admin panel passphrase gate (v3.98.0, `js/ui/DevPanel.js`): F9 / backquote NEVER opens the admin panel directly — it opens the terminal-style `#admin-gate` overlay ("Who is always ready?"). The typed answer is validated case-insensitively (trim + lowercase) via the exported `verifyAdminPassphrase()` against `ADMIN_PASSPHRASES` = `eridaths mom` / `eridath mom` / `em`. Correct → panel opens; wrong → "That is incorrect. your punishment is Back of the line!" with unlimited retries (no lockouts). The gate input swallows keydown (`stopPropagation`) so the game `InputManager` never sees typed keys; Escape/F9/backquote cancel the gate. Behavior is pinned by `tools/check/sections/06ai-admin-gate.mjs` — keep it in sync with any gate change.
- SEARCH & DESTROY mode (v3.99.0 → v4.3.0, `js/modes/SearchAndDestroy/`): the sector-journey mode is a world-space CAMERA LAYER over the untouched screen-space combat stack — the SAR modules NEVER touch the classic combat layer (PlayerFlight stays sovereign: the camera never writes `player.vx/vy`; `p.freeBounds` opts the ship out of classic wrap/bounce only). v4.0.0 camera model (SectorMap): the DISPLACEMENT-ACCUMULATOR — the ship flies in screen space, its screen offset is tracked against a dead zone (`SAR.CAMERA.DEADZONE_X/Y`), the EXCESS delta is accumulated into world coordinates (`worldX`/`worldY`) and the ship is softly recentered (`SAR.CAMERA.RECENTER` lerp + `CLAMP_MARGIN` screen-edge backstop). v4.3.0 autonomous WORLD MOTION (SectorSpawner `worldMotion` registry, a Map keyed by entity alongside `worldLocked`): drops / asteroids / chasing enemies integrate in SCREEN space (classic stack) but are adopted into the registry so their world position advances by their own screen-space delta (mode `auto`, capped at `WORLD_MOTION_MAX_STEP` = 48 px/frame so boss-wrap/teleport artifacts never reach the world layer) or by a registry-owned fixed world velocity (mode `drift`), then re-projected back to screen via `map.worldToScreen()` after the camera advances — CRITICAL INVARIANT: `prevX/prevY` must track the last RE-PROJECTED screen position, so the camera's own shift is never counted as entity motion (setting them pre-re-projection re-introduces compounding drift on sustained scroll — pinned by the 06aj "sustained camera scroll" regression test). v4.3.0 MULTI-LAYER PARALLAX STARFIELD (SectorMap, `SAR.STARFIELD`): tiled `FAR`/`MID`/`NEAR` star layers + `NEBULA` mid-depth dust + `TRAILS` foreground streaks, each with its own parallax factor + autonomous wind drift, modulo-wrapped in tiled layer space so visible density stays constant across the sector (trails streak opposite the player movement vector `p.vx/p.vy`). Sector content is WORLD-ANCHORED at absolute world coordinates (deterministic seeded layout: `debrisAnchors` / `hazardAnchors` / `patrolSites` in SectorMap, activated by camera proximity in SectorSpawner). All SAR tunables live ONLY in `SAR` / `sarProgress` / `sarZoneFor` in `js/core/config/searchDestroy.js` (re-exported by `config.js`) — SAR modules must not hardcode them. Eridath's Mom's House: the 512px native `C:\AI-GAMES\.assets\Eridaths-Moms-House.png` (manifest key `eridath_moms_house`), drawn 512×512 with a `SAR.HOUSE.radius` collision circle, persistent in the deep sector, shootable (off-screen kill gate parity), destroying it wins (`game.victory()` → GameOver "MISSION ACCOMPLISHED"). Entry: `#sard-btn` / `#dev-sard` → `game.start(theme, { mode: 'sard' })`; `Game.js` ticks `game.sard.update(dt)` (frame order: classic player/enemy/powerup integration FIRST, then `sard.update` = camera → spawner world-motion → combat → radar), render swaps in the sector background + radar HUD (RadarManager, F1), `game.sard.hudLabel()` owns the wave label in SAR mode. Pinned by `tools/check/sections/06aj-search-destroy.mjs` — keep it in sync with any SAR change.
- Dynamic procedural soundtrack (v4.4.0, `js/core/AudioSystem.js` + `js/core/game/MusicDirector.js`): the old 4-note A-minor loop is GONE — the mission soundtrack is a zero-file WebAudio generative engine with four context modes (`open` / `combat` / `boneyard` / `boss`), each with its own 8-bar chord progression, tempo, layered pad/arpeggio/bass/percussion and per-phrase seeded variation (3 arpeggio pattern variants rotated per 128-step phrase + pad filter sweep + phrase fills). `audio.setMusicMode(mode)` is the only mode API — it applies at the next bar boundary with a riser (intensity up) / sub-drop (intensity down) accent and is a no-op when unchanged (safe to call every frame, headless-safe). `js/core/game/MusicDirector.js` `syncMusicMode(game)` derives the mode each frame — SAR: OPEN SPACE → `open` (≥5 live enemies → `combat`), THE BONEYARD → `boneyard` (≥9 → `boss`), DEEP SECTOR → `boss` when Eridath's Mom's House is alive and within `SAR.HOUSE.spawnRange` else `combat`; classic: Bone Yard bonus → `boneyard`, Internet boss stage → `boss`, active wave with live enemies → `combat`, else `open` — and is called from `Game.update()`. SFX (shoot/hit/explosion/coin/powerup/banner/superWeapon/gameOver/uiBlip) and the PauseMenu start/stop + setVolumes lifecycle are unchanged.
- Pause menu RETURN TO HANGAR (v4.5.0, `js/ui/PauseMenu.js` + `js/core/game/StageFlow.js`): the ⌂ `#pause-hangar` button in the pause overlay calls `game.returnToHangar()` **directly — never `this.close()` first** (closing first restarts the mission music and re-requests pointer lock, then the teardown releases it again — pure churn). `returnToHangar(game)` in `StageFlow.js` is the single teardown path: active-stage cleanup hook + slot free, all entity arrays (enemies/bullets/powerups/bonusTargets/fireZones/enemyHazards), `hazards.reset()` + `particles.clear()`, player ships (P1 + P2), co-op/LAN (`coopManager.stop()` / `clientMirror.stop()` only when active), SAR facade (`game.sard.destroy()` + `game.mode = 'classic'`), score/multiplier/nextLifeAt/shake/godMode, dev state (aimbot reset, test aimbot off, HUD floaters, msglog clear), stage manifest (`levelRegistry.reset()` + `waveManager.reset()`), `audio.stopMusic()`, `game.state = 'menu'`, `syncCursor(game)` (releases pointer lock — the menu never locks) and the null-safe DOM swap (hide HUD/FC dashboard/pause overlay/game-over, show `#menu-screen`). The permanent `requestAnimationFrame` loop is NEVER stopped — the state machine transitions back to the hangar (menu starfield keeps rendering). Behavior is pinned by `tools/check/sections/06am-pause-hangar.mjs` — keep it in sync with any teardown change.
- Audio modular layout (v4.9.0, `js/core/audio/` E6 tree): the AudioSystem monolith is SPLIT — `AudioCore.js` (lazy AudioContext init/resume, master chain `masterGain → DynamicsCompressor → destination`, SFX/music buses, the master/sfx/music volume knobs + global mute — the SINGLE place volume/mute are enforced), `SoundEffects.js` (all standalone SFX voices; tracked `setTimeout`s + live-source GC via `onended`), `MusicScheduler.js` (the SINGLE mission-music scheduler: ONE lookahead timer + ONE session graph; `start()` ALWAYS hard-kills any previous session — `stop({hard:true})` clears the lookahead timer, cancels the pending teardown timer, force-stops live sources and disconnects the graph — before a new track begins; `stop()` is graceful: master fade + TRACKED teardown timer), `MusicPlaylists.js` (pure data: `MUSIC_MODES`, the 13-song `SONGS` album, per-mode `PLAYLISTS`, the Für Elise + Johnny Marching Home crossover motifs, `hz`/`mulberry32`), `SynthVoice.js` (v4.9.0 POLYPHONIC SYNTH ENGINE — pure voice builders, no state/timers/AudioContext at import: `makeVoice()` = N detuned oscillators + optional sine sub → optional soft-clip WaveShaper → resonant lowpass (optional sweep) → StereoPanner → full ADSR → dest + sends (delay/reverb); `makeChord()` = one voice per chord tone with spread stereo image + per-note detune drift; `kick()`/`snare()`/`hat()` percussion; `makeNoiseBuffer()`/`makeImpulse()`/`softClipCurve()`; every builder RETURNS its started source nodes so callers `_track()` them for teardown). MusicScheduler builds every music voice with it (pads/leads/harmony/arps/stabs/bass/perc through the session graph: layer buses, bass soft-clip + sidechain pump, perc punch comp, procedural convolver reverb, feedback delay) and SoundEffects builds every SFX voice with it. `js/core/AudioSystem.js` is the FACADE — it must keep the exact public `audio` singleton API (`tone/uiBlip/shoot/hit/explosion/coin/powerup/banner/superWeapon/gameOver/startMusic/stopMusic/setMusicMode/getMusicMode/getMusicSong/setVolumes` + `stopAllMusic()`/`resetAudioEngine()`/`setMuted()`) and re-export `VERSION`/`MUSIC_MODES`/`SONGS`/`PLAYLISTS` — every consumer imports `{ audio } from '.../AudioSystem.js'` unchanged. INVARIANTS: never add a second scheduler timer or session graph (one `_timer` + one `_teardownTimer` + one `_master`/`_layers` in MusicScheduler); every source node must be `_track()`ed (auto-removed on `onended`) so teardown can force-stop it; no raw-oscillator music/SFX voices — route them through the SynthVoice.js builders (the only raw sources are the session-graph noise sweeps in MusicScheduler); new music modules live in `js/core/audio/` only — the game-side mode sync stays in `js/core/game/MusicDirector.js` (it calls `audio.setMusicMode()` and owns NO audio nodes). Behavior is pinned by `tools/check/sections/06an-audio-modular.mjs` — keep it in sync with any audio change.
- Primary-weapon master bus (v4.13.0, `js/core/audio/SoundEffects.js`): every Catship **primary-weapon fire voice** (`vulkanShot` / `pulseShot` / `railShot`) routes through the dedicated WEAPON BUS — `WEAPON_BUS_GAIN = 0.65` (a ~35% reduction, keep it in the 0.6–0.7 range) on a lazily-built GainNode (`_weaponBus(ctx)`, cached per AudioContext like the noise buffers) wired into the SFX bus — so continuous Gatling fire blends under the music bed + impact SFX. Weapon fire voices connect to `this._weaponBus(ctx)`, NEVER the raw `this.core.sfxBus`; non-weapon SFX (shoot() rocket whoosh, hit, explosion, UI blips, …) stay on the raw SFX bus. The v4.13.0 `vulkanShot()` is a fast, HEAVY, dual-layer mechanical snap — a low-mid transient click (180–270 Hz square "thock", ~25 ms) under a punchy noise burst (480–820 Hz bandpass casing pop, ~45 ms), both with subtle per-shot pitch variance (bandpass center + playbackRate jitter) — the high-pitched screech/chirp (1800–2700 Hz bandpass + 1500–2000 Hz click) is GONE and must never return; total voice life stays under the 70 ms Gatling cadence. Behavior is pinned by `tools/check/sections/06aq-weapon-sfx-balance.mjs` — keep it in sync with any weapon SFX change.
- MIDI ALBUM import pipeline (v4.16.0, `tools/midi-import.mjs`): the entire `SONGS` soundtrack in `js/core/audio/MusicPlaylists.js` is GENERATED, never hand-edited — the zero-dependency SMF parser reads the local `.mid` files in `C:\AI-GAMES\.assets\`, classifies each MIDI channel into a SynthVoice.js voice slot (lead/bass/arp/pad/drums; GM percussion map for ch 10, pitch-range heuristics for the melodic channels, and per-track `chMap` overrides that pin the MAIN melody to the lead slot — the auto-classify sends a dense polyphonic mid-range channel to the quiet pad, so the real melody must be pinned), and writes every note onto the MusicScheduler 32nd-note grid (`events: { lead/bass/arp/pad: [[t, midiNote, dur32nds, vel01]], drums: [[t, kind, vel01]] }` with kind 0 kick / 1 snare / 2 closed hat / 3 open hat). Genre `PROFILES` (metal / ballad / classical / march / synth / piano) set each track's lead + bass voice config, the layer `vols` (pad/arp/lead/bass/perc — the drums `perc` gain must stay well under the melodic layers or the track sounds drum-heavy), and `padCutoff`. To change the album: edit the `TRACKS` lineup / `chMap` / `PROFILES` in `tools/midi-import.mjs`, then re-run `node tools/midi-import.mjs --write` (use `--report` for a per-channel audit: note count, pitch range, polyphony, role). The `.mid` sources are tracked in `C:\AI-GAMES\.assets\` (the PNGs there are gitignored). The admin jukebox is a single `#dev-jukebox` `<select>` (DevPanel.js builds one `<option>` per SONGS track; picking one previews via `audio.previewSong`, and STOP / gameplay `startMusic()` reset it to the placeholder). Pinned by `tools/check/sections/06an-audio-modular.mjs` (note counts + the melody-in-lead fidelity gate) + `06ao-audio-suite-v411.mjs` (the dropdown picker) — keep them in sync with any import / jukebox change.
- Per-track mix + v4.21.0 audio tuning (v4.19.0 → v4.21.0, `js/core/audio/MusicPlaylists.js` + `MusicScheduler.js`): `TRACK_MIX_SETTINGS` is the per-song mix table — one entry per SONGS key with FIVE positive scalars `gainLead / gainBass / gainDrums / gainArp / gainPad` (v4.20.0 added `gainArp` + `gainPad`; the MusicScheduler event path multiplies all five into the per-layer gains, so every track needs all five keys). **Forty Six & 2 (`tool-forty-six`) is the volume reference and stays all 1.0** — tune the other tracks against it. v4.21.0 re-tuned values (the "most tracks are ~2x too quiet" pass): axel-f L4/B2/D1.5/A2.5/P2.5 (the hook rides arp+pad at base vol 0.05/0.06 — it was inaudible), metallica-unforgiven L2.5/B1.8/D1/A2.5/P1.5 (rhythm guitar + "synth" harmony were buried), tool-pneuma L2/B1.5/D1/A2.2/P1.5, johnny-march L3/B1.5/D0.2/A0.8/P1 (the melody over the march snare), ozzy-crazy-train L4, eiffel65-blue L3.5, fur-elise L3.5, tool-no-quarter L3.5, metallica-nem L3/B1.5/D1.5, requiem-dream L3/D0.8/A2, pantera-cowboys L3/B2/D1.5, metallica-harvester L3/D0.9/A1.5, classical-gas L3, black-sabbath-cotg L2.5/B1.5/D0.8. **v4.21.0 SONGS PLAY OUT**: `MusicScheduler.setMode()` only records `_pendingMode` — the pending mode applies at the current song's END (`finalBar`), never at a bar boundary, so open↔combat flips no longer cut songs mid-play; the riser/sub-drop transition accent plays on the song handoff. **v4.21.0 per-song ARP voice profile**: a `song.arp` object (`{ wave, detunes, lp, q, adsr }`) overrides the genre profile's arp voice in `_pluckNote()` — `tool-pneuma` rides `arp: { wave: 'sawtooth', detunes: [-8, 0, 8], lp: 2600, q: 1.1, adsr: { a: 0.01, d: 0.12, s: 0.6, r: 0.1 } }` (its 2514-note power-chord rhythm is a sustained saw guitar, not a dead triangle pluck). `black-sabbath-cotg` is the OPENING track (`PLAYLISTS.open[0]`, still in the boss queue) and `metallica-nem` rides the `piano` profile (the ballad saw+sub "gross synth" lead is gone — do not restore it). EXCEPTION: while `C:\AI-GAMES\.assets` is unreadable (v4.20.0 → v4.21.0), the mix values + arp profile were hand-edited in `MusicPlaylists.js` AND `tools/midi-import.mjs` (each `TRACKS` entry's `mix` object + `arp` profile) in lockstep — re-run the importer once the `.mid` files are reachable again so the two stay in sync. Pinned by `tools/check/sections/06an-audio-modular.mjs` (5-scalar table + v4.21.0 tuned values + songs-play-out + per-song arp profile + NEM piano profile + CoTG opening track).
- Cannon SFX de-pitch (v4.20.0, `js/core/audio/SoundEffects.js`): the Pulse + Rail cannon voices dropped ~40% so they no longer sound like toys — `pulseShot()` energy core is a 520→105 Hz sweep (was 900→180 Hz) with the zap click at 1400→520 Hz (was 2400→900 Hz), and `railShot()` discharge zing is 1100→3200 Hz (was the toy-bright 2800→7500 Hz) with the crack highpass at 3200 Hz (was 4500 Hz). Do not restore the old bright frequencies; the vulkan voice (180–270 Hz thock + 480–820 Hz pop) is unchanged. Pinned by `tools/check/sections/06aq-weapon-sfx-balance.mjs` — keep it in sync with any weapon SFX change.
- Core UI managers (v4.29.0, `js/core/ui/`): standalone screen-level UI managers live in `js/core/ui/` (first: `AdBannerManager.js` — the Eridath's Mom Enterprises lower-left ad banner). They build their OWN DOM (no index.html container needed — index.html only carries the settings toggle) and MUST be Node-safe: probe `document.createElement('canvas').getContext('2d')` before building any DOM so `tools/check.mjs` can import them headless (the check shim's stub elements have no `getContext`). The ad banner is a STANDALONE overlay in the TRUE lower-left CORNER of the main game screen (left:14px / bottom:14px, z-index 30, joke size 240px / 64×64 sprite) — NEVER merge it into the fire-control panel markup. v4.29.1 pop-up model: the banner STARTS HIDDEN and pops up with a NEW ad every 30–60 s (random), stays on screen 12 s, then retracts (constants `POPUP_MIN_MS` / `POPUP_MAX_MS` / `VISIBLE_MS`). The minimize button (–) is REAL: it retracts the banner and docks an "AD · MOM" chip (`#ad-dock`) into the minimized fire-control bar (`#fc-mini-bar`, appended at runtime by `_buildDock()`) so nothing floats; clicking the chip restores the ad — close/maximize stay fake (toast only). Its enable toggle is Settings → MONETIZATION / AD BANNERS (`#set-ads`, default ON) bound by `SettingsScreen._buildAds()`; the banner owns its own `kitty_enable_ads` localStorage key (NOT Settings.js's `kve-settings-v1` blob) and `setEnabled(bool)` must turn the pop-up cycle on/off immediately (off = hide + undock + clear timers) and persist. Ad copy lives ONLY in `AD_CATALOG` (extensible `{ id, title, subtitle, body, sprite, cta }` objects; `sprite` = AssetSprites.js registry key, scaled nearest-neighbor). Pinned by `tools/check/sections/06au-ad-banner.mjs` — keep it in sync with any ad-banner change.
